# Architecture Rules

## Layered Architecture

```
Presentation (src/app/, src/features/) → Application (src/application/) → Domain (src/domain/)
Infrastructure (src/infrastructure/) implements Application ports
```

**Dependencies point inward only.** Domain depends on nothing.

## Critical Boundaries

- `src/domain/` — Pure TypeScript. NO imports from React, Next.js, Drizzle, HTTP, or any framework.
- `src/application/` — May import `src/domain/` only. Defines port interfaces.
- `src/infrastructure/` — Implements ports. May import domain + application types. NO React/Next.js.
- `src/features/` and `src/app/` — Presentation layer. Consume application use cases.

## Business Logic Location

- Domain services: `src/domain/services/` (pure logic: progression, volume, exercise selection)
- Use cases: `src/application/use-cases/` (orchestration: complete workout, enroll in program)
- NEVER in React components, Server Actions, Route Handlers, or DB queries.

## Project Structure

```
src/
├── app/              # Next.js routes, layouts, pages
├── domain/           # Pure domain (entities, value-objects, services, types)
├── application/      # Use cases, ports, DTOs
├── infrastructure/   # Database, auth, AI integrations
├── features/         # Feature UI (components, actions, hooks, schemas)
├── components/       # Shared UI (ui/ = shadcn, shared/ = composites)
├── lib/              # Utilities, Result type, errors
└── types/            # Shared types
```

## Key Rules

1. Server Components by default. Client Components only for interactivity, kept small and leaf-level.
2. Server Actions validate with Zod, delegate to use cases, return Result.
3. Repositories map DB rows ↔ Domain objects. Components never see DB types.
4. No ORM imports outside `src/infrastructure/database/`.
5. Feature components in `src/features/[name]/components/`. Shared in `src/components/`.

See `AGENTS.md` and `docs/architecture.md` for full details.